/// Adapts a provider [StreamFunction] into a [HideJudgeFn].
///
/// Mirrors [streamFunctionSummarizer]: a standalone request with the
/// judge system prompt plus the ledger as a single user message,
/// `cacheRetention: 'none'`, fresh routing session id; returns the joined
/// text blocks or `null` on error/abort/empty (F1). Temperature 0 and
/// `max_tokens` ≥ 1500 (F2) are the model-role/adapter's responsibility —
/// the same place the summarizer's pi clamp divergence lives.
HideJudgeFn streamFunctionHideJudge(
  StreamFunction streamFunction,
  Model model, {
  required String system,
  void Function(String delta)? onDelta,

  /// Aborts the in-flight judge call — the compaction budget owner
  /// cancels it on expiry (issue #515).
  CancelToken? cancelToken,
}) {
  return (String ledgerText) async {
    try {
      final stream = StreamCacheRouting.runWith(
        () => streamFunction(
          model,
          Context(
            systemPrompt: system,
            messages: [UserMessage.text(ledgerText)],
          ),
          cancelToken: cancelToken,
        ),
        sessionId: uuidv7(),
        cacheRetention: 'none',
      );
      if (onDelta != null) {
        stream.listen((event) {
          final delta = switch (event) {
            TextDeltaEvent(:final delta) => delta,
            ThinkingDeltaEvent(:final delta) => delta,
            _ => null,
          };
          if (delta != null && delta.isNotEmpty) onDelta(delta);

The judge calls `streamFunction(model, context)` — that's the wrapper. The wrapper's `call` builds `out` and drives async — the driver selects entries. If the driver errors silently... the print in catchError didn't fire, so `call` was never invoked.

So the compactor NEVER invoked the judge. Which means the structured engine's pass loop decided zero passes AND the classic engine also didn't summarize.

Hmm wait — let me look at the factory once more:

```dart
final outcome = await _runStructured(adapter: adapter, capTriggered: capTriggered);
if (outcome.ok && (adapter.passCount > 0 || !(force || capTriggered))) { ... return ... }
// falls through to classic
``

If structured FAILS (ok=false), falls to classic. Classic: `AutoCompactor.run(force: force || capTriggered)`. Let me check what classic does when forced — maybe it ALSO gates on something that fails here, e.g. `shouldCompact` — no, forced semantics. Let me actually check if classic THREW — `_compactChildIfNeeded` catches everything silently. Print in that catch!

