void _applyDetectedContextWindow(Model model) {
  final detected = _modelContextWindows[model.id];
  if (detected == null) return;
  if (detected != model.contextWindow) {
    _replaceModelLimits(
      contextWindow: detected,
      // gh-1742 invariant 2: the detection publishes into the shared
      // registry so children spawned afterwards ride the SERVED
      // window, not the advertised one.
      windowSource: ContextWindowSource.endpointReport,
    );
    io.writeln(_style.dim('model context window: $detected (from endpoint)'));
  } else {
    contextWindowRegistry.publish(
      model: model,
      window: detected,
      source: ContextWindowSource.endpointReport,
    );
  }
}

/// The explicit fallback when the endpoint answered `/models` but
/// reported NO context window for the active model: the carried value
/// (catalog default, or whatever a previous model left behind) is
/// UNVERIFIED — say so once per model id instead of silently letting
/// the ctx meter, the compaction threshold, and the over-window guard
/// all divide by a number nobody confirmed.
void _noteUndetectedContextWindow(Model model) {
  if (!_undetectedWindowNoteIds.add(model.id)) return;
  io.writeln(
    _style.dim(
      'model context window: ${model.contextWindow} (not reported by the '
      'endpoint; carried default — /model-edit contextWindow <n> to '
      'override)',
    ),
  );
}

/// Applies the endpoint-reported max-tokens cap for [model] when it
/// differs from the carried one (see [_applyDetectedContextWindow]).
void _applyDetectedMaxTokens(Model model) {
  final detectedCap = _modelMaxTokens[model.id];
  if (detectedCap != null && detectedCap != model.maxTokens) {
    _replaceModelLimits(maxTokens: detectedCap);
    io.writeln(_style.dim('model max tokens: $detectedCap (from endpoint)'));
  }
}

{"content":"# Thread 4 — a confirming endpoint report still leaves the window "unverified" (`lib/src/cli/provider_models.dart`)

Fixed exactly as suggested.

**Commit** `b5f0ff7460` — `_applyDetectedContextWindow` now treats the three cases separately:

```dart
if (detected != model.contextWindow) {
  _replaceModelLimits(contextWindow: detected, windowSource: endpointReport);
  io.writeln(_style.dim('model context window: $detected (from endpoint)'));
} else {
  // The endpoint CONFIRMED the carried value: publish it so the AC6
  // verification ladder is honest (windowFor returns what the model
  // already carries — a behavioral no-op, but isVerified flips true).
  contextWindowRegistry.publish(
    model: model,
    window: detected,
    source: ContextWindowSource.endpointReport,
  );
}
```

The confirming path publishes unconditionally into the registry — `windowFor` returns the value
the model already carries and `withRegisteredContextWindow` short-circuits on equality, so the only
observable change is `registry.isVerified(model)` → true and the `task_status` pressure badge
marking the window verified. No "(from endpoint)" dim line is printed for a confirmation (nothing
changed, so nothing to announce).

**Test** (`test/cli/copilot_provider_test.dart`): "an endpoint-reported context window in roles
mode — a CONFIRMING report verifies the registry window" drives a fetch whose reported window
equals the carried one and asserts `contextWindowRegistry.isVerified(model)` is true afterwards.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_4_confirming_report_publishes.md"}

